# rena0-guard-gate-pilot — F1-3 fixture, P2-7 guard family
# The recovered guard gate: a guarded melee hit applies NO damage and no stun.
# `FUN_00637950`'s guarded branch (the `else` at the listing's lines 541-552) writes the
# contact word, the per-slot marker and [victim+0xaf30] and calls no damage helper; the
# predicate is (|bearing - facing| <= 45 || victim 0x2000) && victim 0x400 && !attack 8
# (fighter.h's guard note; the bundle's battle_hit_guard.hpp).
#
# The `pilot rena0-guard` directive attaches the recovered gate to the dummy exactly as
# --native-actions=rena0 does in the live run. Without it, the same scenario pins the legacy
# path (rena0-guard-gate-legacy.fixture) and the two differ only in that directive.
# Body separation off: the dummy is held on the attack volume, inside the 60-unit radius
# (V3-45's open item).
body_separation 0
combo 0 0
seed 5489
spawn 0 0 0 0
spawn 1 0 0 300
collision open-field
dummy_guard 1
pilot rena0-guard
input 0 MELEE
place_at_attack active
expect 15 melee_hit 1
expect 16 dummy_hp 100
expect 16 dummy_ko 0
